{
  "summary": "This experiment tested combining scvi_n200 RNA encoding with ResNet50 image features via concatenation fusion in a multimodal setting, aiming to assess if multimodal integration could enhance performance beyond single-modality baselines. Validation accuracy of 0.5362 (F1: 0.5158) slightly outperforms the previous multimodal baseline (0.5266 accuracy) but remains lower than the RNA-only scvi_n200 baseline (0.6530 accuracy). Uncertainty persists about whether multimodal fusion with this encoder pair can achieve performance gains over single-modality approaches, and whether the concat fusion method contributes meaningfully to the results."
}

